  Summary

  Story: US-007 - Migrate explore/index.svelte to new Feed API

  What was implemented:

  1. Moved subscription handling to parent - The explore page now manages its ow
     ubscription using useSubscription hook from @candypoets/nipworker/hooks
  2. Implemented quantile-based pagination - The handleNearBottom callback calcu
     es the until parameter using the last item's createdAt timestamp
  3. Implemented pull-to-refresh - The handleRefresh callback resets the feed an
     reates a fresh subscription
  4. Used bind:start for scroll tracking - Tracks when the user is at the top (s
     t === 0) vs scrolled down
  5. Managed feed items in parent - feedItems array is now maintained in the par
     component and passed to Feed via items prop
  6. Removed old Feed bindings - Removed bind:feed, subscriptionID, requests, su
     riptionOptions, kinds props

  Key patterns learned:

  • Use useSubscription(subId, requests, handler, options) for Nostr subscriptio
  • Pagination: until = lastItem.createdAt() - 1 creates a sliding window
  • Track new posts using start > 0 (scrolled down) vs start === 0 (at top)
  • Filter arrays with type guards: .filter((p): p is string => typeof p === 'st
    ng')

  Files changed: src/routes/explore/index.svelte

